---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../consts";

import HeroSection from "../components/sections/about/HeroSection.astro";
import WhyWeExistSection from "../components/sections/about/WhyWeExistSection.astro";
import FounderSection from "../components/sections/about/FounderSection.astro";
import HowWeDecideSection from "../components/sections/about/HowWeDecideSection.astro";
import BoundariesSection from "../components/sections/about/BoundariesSection.astro";
import WhoWeWorkWithSection from "../components/sections/about/WhoWeWorkWithSection.astro";
import CloseSection from "../components/sections/about/CloseSection.astro";

/*
 * /about — built Aug 26 2026 against the approved copy in docs/about-page.md. It had
 * been a 404 behind the nav and footer "About" links since the site shipped.
 *
 * ABOUT IS NOT A BIOGRAPHY. It is the page a reader opens when they are close to booking
 * and want to know whether the firm behind the argument is credible. The copy file gives
 * it three questions to answer, and then to stop:
 *
 *   1. What is this firm?            An AI consulting firm — assess, quantify, build.
 *   2. Who am I dealing with?        The founder, directly, with a verifiable record.
 *   3. How do they decide what to build?  Assessment first, and a stated willingness to
 *                                    recommend nothing.
 *
 * Anything that does not serve one of those three does not belong here.
 *
 * THE ONE RULE FOR THIS PAGE: it speaks as "we" throughout, and Fredrick is named once,
 * in the third person, written ABOUT rather than BY. That single choice is what makes the
 * page read as a company with a founder rather than a person with a website, and it is
 * the thing most likely to drift during an edit — section 3's second paragraph attracts
 * an "I" more than anything else on the site. It has none. Keep it that way.
 *
 * Seven sections, in the copy file's order:
 *
 *   1  Hero                 what the firm is. NO CTA, by instruction
 *   2  Why we exist         the position: the tools aren't the constraint
 *   3  Who you're working with  the founder, and the portrait. No portrait, no section
 *   4  How we decide        prose and a pull quote. No steps, no diagram
 *   5  What we don't do     four boundaries
 *   6  Who we work with     the fit, and the link to /accounting
 *   7  Close                the only CTA on the page
 *
 * ONE CTA, IN THE CLOSE, labelled about-closing. The hero deliberately carries none: a
 * reader who opens About is verifying, not deciding, and a button at the top interrupts
 * exactly what they came to do. If a second CTA ever appears on this page, something has
 * gone wrong with it.
 *
 * NO ILLUSTRATIONS. The founder portrait in section 3 is the only image, by instruction,
 * and there is no stepper or process diagram anywhere — a staged treatment makes the
 * engagement feel long and duplicates what /accounting and /workshop already do. Every
 * section therefore has to carry its own band without artwork, which is why 1, 2 and 6
 * run two-column heads, 4 leans on a full-width pull quote, and 5 runs a 2x2.
 *
 * "METRO VANCOUVER" IS REMOVED FROM ALL THREE VISIBLE PLACES the approved copy puts it —
 * the hero subhead, section 3's fourth chip, and section 6's location paragraph, which
 * went whole rather than half-kept. Fredrick's instruction of Aug 25 2026 takes the
 * location line and everything like it off the visible site; he confirmed it again on
 * Aug 26 when this page was planned, having been shown that this copy restored it. The
 * TITLE AND META DESCRIPTION KEEP IT, which is the same call made for the other two
 * pages: a title tag is a search-targeting string rather than a sentence on a page, and
 * "AI consultant Metro Vancouver" is one of this page's four target queries.
 *
 * One consequence worth knowing: the on-site-in-the-Lower-Mainland offer existed only in
 * section 6's deleted paragraph and is now published nowhere on the site.
 *
 * SECTION 3 IS THE LONG VERSION OF THE HOMEPAGE FOUNDER STRIP and the two share their
 * heading, body paragraph and chips word for word. THEY HAVE TO STAY IN SYNC — a change
 * to the years, the products or the chips here is wrong on the homepage the same day,
 * and there is no shared constant because it is prose, not data.
 *
 * "A GUESS WITH AN INVOICE ATTACHED" in section 2 is a phrase Fredrick cut from the
 * homepage on Aug 25. It is deliberate here and was flagged before this page was built —
 * see the note in WhyWeExistSection.astro for why the two uses are different. Do not
 * delete it as a duplicate of the homepage fix.
 *
 * Schema: AboutPage and Organization. The copy file asks for the Organization block to
 * live here specifically, because this is the page search engines should read as the
 * entity definition. The homepage's own Organization node stays where it is — they are
 * per-page nodes describing the same entity, not a conflict.
 *
 * sameAs IS STILL ABSENT. The copy file elsewhere specifies LinkedIn; the URL is not in
 * the repo and a guessed profile URL is worse than none, because it is a claim about
 * identity. Add the real one to the founder node and the organization node together when
 * it is supplied.
 *
 * LocalBusiness is NOT emitted, here least of all. It needs a real street address and
 * real hours, and this page has just had its location line removed — emitting a postal
 * address in the markup while declining to print it on the page would be incoherent as
 * well as invented.
 *
 * FOUR THINGS THE COPY FILE FLAGS FOR CONFIRMATION. Two are closed, two are Fredrick's:
 *
 *   1. FOUNDER PORTRAIT — CLOSED. assets/fred.jpg, already live on the homepage.
 *   2. ON-SITE RADIUS — CLOSED, by removal. The paragraph that carried it is gone.
 *   3. TEAM LANGUAGE. The page says "the people who build your system" and "we"
 *      throughout while naming one founder. Defensible as written whether or not anyone
 *      else works on delivery; flagged so the plural is a choice rather than an accident.
 *   4. FoodyGuru AND YoseeAI. Both are already named on the homepage, so this page adds
 *      no new exposure — but confirm neither has a live state that contradicts "founded
 *      and shipped", which is the deliberately unarguable phrasing and must not be
 *      inflated.
 */

const aboutSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  name: "About ArkSystems",
  url: `${SITE.url}/about`,
  description:
    "ArkSystems is an AI consulting firm. We establish where AI produces a return in a business, what it is worth, and whether the build is justified — then build it.",
};

const organizationSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Organization",
  name: SITE.name,
  url: SITE.url,
  description:
    "AI consulting firm. We establish where AI produces a return in a business, quantify it, and build it. Assessment first, business case second, build only if the case holds.",
  founder: {
    "@type": "Person",
    name: "Fredrick",
    jobTitle: "Founder",
  },
  areaServed: {
    "@type": "AdministrativeArea",
    name: "Canada",
  },
  /* sameAs is specified in the copy files as pointing at LinkedIn. The URL is not in the
   * repo, and a guessed profile URL is worse than none — it is a claim about identity.
   * Add the real one here and to the founder node above at the same time. */
};
---

{/*
  Title and description are the approved strings from docs/about-page.md, used character
  for character — the file counted them (49 and 147) and the separator is part of what it
  counted, which is why this goes through titleOverride rather than being rebuilt from
  the site's em-dash pattern.

  BOTH KEEP "Vancouver" while the visible page does not, and that is deliberate rather
  than an oversight — Fredrick's decision of Aug 26 2026, the same call made for the
  other two pages. A title tag and a meta description are search-targeting strings, and
  two of this page's four target queries name the location. No sentence rendered on the
  page names a place.
*/}
<BaseLayout
  title="About ArkSystems"
  titleOverride="About ArkSystems | AI Consulting, Vancouver"
  description="ArkSystems is an AI consulting firm in Metro Vancouver. We establish where AI produces a return in your operation, what it's worth, and then build it."
>
  <script
    slot="head"
    type="application/ld+json"
    set:html={JSON.stringify(aboutSchema)}
    is:inline
  />
  <script
    slot="head"
    type="application/ld+json"
    set:html={JSON.stringify(organizationSchema)}
    is:inline
  />

  <HeroSection />
  <WhyWeExistSection />
  <FounderSection />
  <HowWeDecideSection />
  <BoundariesSection />
  <WhoWeWorkWithSection />
  <CloseSection />
</BaseLayout>
